v0.11.2: orchestra registry — first-class membership with admin-gated joins

Confirmed with Ivan first: the football-manager model. Fermi's
Brier is roster-locked (lives in forecasts made by this team),
but Fermi's manager skill is roster-orthogonal (Team − Counterfactual
isolates the synthesis contribution). This release owns the roster
substrate; counterfactual computation is a placeholder column.

Change:

  Migration 172 — orchestra_membership_requests table + views
  ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  * orchestra_membership_requests (audit trail: pending/approved/
    rejected/withdrawn, reviewer + note + proposed_contract)
  * VIEW orchestra_fermi_members     — published + fermi_contract set
  * VIEW orchestra_xaman_ek_members  — every published agent (implicit)
  * fermi_forecasts.counterfactual_brier (nullable placeholder for
    the manager-effect metric)

  src/handlers/orchestras.rs (new)
  ────────────────────────────────
  Seven endpoints, all governance-gated:

    GET  /api/orchestras                              # list + counts
    GET  /api/orchestras/:name/members                # full roster
    GET  /api/orchestras/:name/requests               # admin inbox
    POST /api/orchestras/:name/requests               # submit (owner)
    POST /api/orchestras/:name/requests/:id/approve   # admin
    POST /api/orchestras/:name/requests/:id/reject    # admin (note req'd)
    POST /api/orchestras/:name/requests/:id/withdraw  # requester
    GET  /api/agents/:id/orchestras                   # per-agent

  Owner-gate on submit (agent's owner or platform admin).
  Admin-gate on approve/reject: owner of strategist agent card
  (for fermi, whoever owns the `fermi` card) OR platform admin.
  Transactional approve: sets fermi_contract + updates request +
  writes admin_bypass_events audit row in one tx. Partial state
  is impossible.

  templates/agent_detail.html
  ────────────────────────────
  New Orchestras section on the Manage tab. Shows current
  memberships + pending requests per orchestra. "Request
  Membership" button on Fermi opens a three-prompt flow
  (finding_labels, multiplier_range, rationale) then submits.
  Pending requests show admin's review note inline.

  schema_trust manifest extended
  ──────────────────────────────
  New table + 8 columns + counterfactual_brier added. v0.11.0
  boot check would surface any drift.

Governance model (the football-manager framing, locked):
  roster-locked:      Fermi Brier IS the team's Brier
  roster-orthogonal:  Manager skill = Team − Counterfactual Brier
                      (same roster, without cep_weighted synthesis)

  This release: roster substrate.
  Next release:  counterfactual computation + delta.

Not in scope (v0.11.3+ candidates):
  * Admin-inbox UI page (approve via curl for now)
  * Counterfactual Brier computation
  * Wire Fermi's dispatcher to query orchestra_fermi_members view
  * Wire xaman_ek's list_agents to query orchestra_xaman_ek_members
  * Additional orchestras (simops, coherence)

The last two are agent-card / prompt tuning, not infra. The
substrate is done here.

